okay every once in a while I like to  look at what the betting money has to  say about what's going to happen in  November of 2020 and there's something  interesting which is that if you pull  people and say who do you support in an  election you get one set of results and  that's the way typical polling is done  you can do the polls a different way  which is you can say regardless of who  you support who do you think will  ultimately win an election and you often  get different results and very often  they are quite accurate one way that  people show who they believe is going to  win is by betting money in prediction  markets which you can do online and in  the last 48 hours something very  interesting has happened the money now  has Bernie Sanders as the most likely to  be Democratic nominee again this is not  who supports Bernie it's what are people  betting on in terms of who will be the  Democratic nominee and it still has  Donald Trump's re-election as the most  likely single outcome in fact  significantly spiking as well over the  last little while so let me explain all  of this predict wise is a website that  aggregates the betting on different  betting websites oftentimes thinking in  bets is a good idea to clarify how  confident we are in our belief that  something will or won't happen so for me  to say Bernie's going to be the nominee  or he won't of course I can't have 100%  certainty that he will or that he won't  so sometimes when you think about it as  a bet you're assigning some level of  confidence so for example if I have 60  percent certainty that Bernie would be  the nominee I might be willing to bet a  hundred dollars to win a hundred and  sixty dollars on that bed right I'm  making up these numbers or if I'm not  super confident I might be willing to  risk $100 or only if I were to win 400  if I was right because my confidence is  lower so I've got to have more possibly  coming my way raising the expected value  of the bet the math doesn't really  matter except to say that a lot of  people are betting on these outcomes and  over the last six weeks the money  betting that Trump  we'll be the eventual winner of the  November 20 2011 has gone up quite a bit  and is now at 53 percent 53 percent of  all the money being bet says Trump gets  reelected the next most likely outcomes  are 14 percent believe Biden will be the  next president 14 percent believe Bernie  will be the next president much smaller  percentages for other candidates now for  the Democratic nomination over the last  few days the numbers have hugely spiked  for Bernie Sanders putting him in the  lead 31% of the betting believes Bernie  will be the nominee taking a lead over  28 percent who believe it will be Joe  Biden 11 percent say Bloomberg and 10  percent say Warren so as you can see  these numbers are not the polling  numbers Bloomberg at 11 percent is way  over representative / representative  represented relative to the 5 percent  that he's polling because again these  are prediction markets this is not who  do you support it's based on all factors  that you consider who do you think will  ultimately win so what has caused this  there's probably a number of factors  number one Bernie taking a lead last  week in the historically important Des  Moines Register poll of Iowa voters has  certainly helped him in the prediction  markets Bernie taking a lead in a number  of recent California polls California is  an important state for the primary many  delegates Bernie leading in two of the  last three polls there to some degree it  appears that the Bernie said a woman  can't win attack that Fiasco may have  failed and Bernie may not be as  vulnerable as some might think to such a  smear campaign and that may have helped  him in the prediction markets as well  although I'm sure there will be more  attack attempts in the coming months now  there's an important statistical reality  that we have to contend with here you  hear a lot of Bernie supporters say  Bernie's the only one who can beat Trump  many people say this about whoever they  support we have Bernie supporters who  say Bernie's the only one that can win I  have yang supporters who say Yang's the  only one that can win I have tulsi  supporters who say she's the only one  that can win not so much about Biden but  the idea is a lot of people say to me  the person ice  Court is the only one who can defeat  Donald Trump in the betting markets note  that as Bernie's nomination has become  more and more likely based on the  betting trump's reelection has also  become more and more likely in terms of  the betting so it may be different  people betting on each but we have to  contend with the reality that as more  and more people believe Bernie will be  the nominee more and more people believe  Trump will be re-elected President of  the United States given the historical  accuracy of the betting markets we may  not want to ignore this although of  course nothing is set in stone and  trying to defeat an incumbent like  Donald Trump is different than anything  that we've seen in American political  history so let me know what you think  about this and specifically here's the  question I want you to answer why have  the betting odds for a Trump reelection  increased in parallel with the betting  odds for a Bernie Democratic nomination  I want to hear from you we will follow  up about this on the David Pakman show  Instagram please make sure you're  following it at David Pakman show and  while you're there give me a follow I  posted some unhinged hate mail this  morning that I got I'm David Pakman on  Instagram
 

